-- The §-INVOCATION exhibit (DMN-EXPORT-PROGRAM-MODEL-SPEC.md §2.3, §13.5):
-- the ONE construct on which the two flavors emit different bytes, isolated
-- in its own module so every other golden can stay unsuffixed.
--
-- `special rate` is deliberately NOT a BKM: @nonexhaustive puts it in the
-- safety-refused set (§6.2's boundary — an uncertified body is never emitted
-- as a BKM). It IS §-invocable: the sole output of its § `special assessment`,
-- whose service encapsulates `assessment floor` and whose inputs are exactly
-- the decide's own GIVEN parameters. So the call in `special case`:
--
--   * on the `kie` flavor renders as the decisionService invocation
--     `special_assessment(p: 150, q: 5)`, with a knowledgeRequirement →
--     decisionService edge on the caller — REQUIRED by KIE (compile error
--     without it, probe D3);
--   * on the `camunda` flavor stays raw L4 with a Blocking
--     D-FLAVOR-NOSERVICE note, because that same edge is FATAL to Camunda 8's
--     parse() (§13.4, probe D2). The camunda golden of this exhibit is
--     therefore UNLOADABLE on its own flavor's engine — that is the exhibit:
--     the flavor REFUSES the construct, and the refusal is loud in the
--     fidelity report rather than silent in the artifact.
--
-- Goldens: svc.dmn (camunda, unsuffixed) + svc.kie.dmn — the first
-- flavor-SPLIT golden pair (§13.6). The flavor-divergence tests in
-- jl4/tests/DmnExport.hs and jl4/tests-cli/Main.hs assert the split
-- positively on this subject: the kie bytes contain a requiredKnowledge
-- pointing at a decisionService and the camunda bytes do not.

IMPORT prelude

§ `Service exhibit`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`base charge` MEANS 40

GIVETH A NUMBER
`special case` MEANS `special rate` 150 5 PLUS `base charge`

§§ `special assessment`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`assessment floor` MEANS 100

-- @nonexhaustive is the REFUSAL LEVER, not a fact about the chain (it has an
-- OTHERWISE): the decorator puts the decide in the L2 safety set, which keeps
-- it out of the emitted-BKM population and in the §-invocable one. Both
-- engines still evaluate it standalone.
@nonexhaustive
GIVEN p IS A NUMBER
      q IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`special rate` p q MEANS
    BRANCH IF p GREATER THAN `assessment floor` THEN p PLUS q
           OTHERWISE p MINUS q
